  "overview": {
    "title": "Clear water near town",
    "p1": "Cala Bonita is a small, sheltered cove a short hop from Al Hoceima’s centre — clearer water and a more intimate scale than the main Quemado strip.",
    "p2": "The mix of pebbles and sand, plus cliff backdrop, makes it popular for swimming when the sea is calm. Space is limited compared with Sfiha or Quemado.",
    "p3": "Arrive earlier in summer for room on the shore. Combine with Quemado or a corniche evening rather than treating it as a full-day destination alone."
  },
